# Frontend (React + Vite)

## Structure

- Types: `frontend/src/types.ts`
- HTTP: `frontend/src/api/client.ts` only (no raw `fetch` in components)
- UI: `components/` with colocated `*.module.css`
- State for list/create/edit/filters lives in `App.tsx` unless a change needs more

## API contract

- Base URL: `VITE_API_BASE_URL` or `http://127.0.0.1:8000`
- Paths: `/tasks`; fields: `title`, `status`, `priority`, `due_date`; list key `tasks`
- Surface failures with `ApiError` / parent error props (same pattern as today)

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — go through the client
const created = await createTask({ title })

// ❌ BAD — fetch inside a component
await fetch('http://127.0.0.1:8000/tasks', { ... })
```

## UI conventions

- Functional components; CSS modules (not new CSS frameworks unless asked).
- Preserve the current dashboard visual language (stats, filters, **Your tasks**).
- Keep Vite `server.host` as `127.0.0.1` so `http://127.0.0.1:5173` works on Windows.
